   "notes": [
    "Note 5: the output can carry up to 20 mA whatever VCC is; a short from the output to VCC can overheat the part until it fails.",
    "Note 6: measured at the output switching point, VO ≈ 1.4 Vdc, with RS = 0 Ω; it holds over a 5.0 Vdc to 30 Vdc supply and with the inputs anywhere between 0 V and VCC - 1.5 V.",
    "Note 7: the inputs are PNP transistors, so bias current flows out of the input pins. It stays nearly the same in either output state, so the load the inputs put on the source does not change when the output switches.",
    "Note 8: neither input should be taken more than 0.3 V below ground (or the negative supply); the inputs work up to VCC - 1.5 V at most.",
    "Note 9: response time is for a 100 mV input step with 5.0 mV of overdrive; more overdrive makes the response faster.",
    "Note 10: one input may rise above VCC and the output still gives the right state, provided the other input stays inside the common mode range. The lower input must stay above -0.3 V with respect to ground or the negative supply."
